# `client/ui` — portable, domain-free presentation (`@21n/ui`)

Charter: reusable UI that knows nothing about this product. It must be droppable
into any product or extension unchanged.

## Layers (import direction is one-way, top depends on bottom)

- `compositions` — compound UI built from primitives (charts, maps, breadcrumbs,
  nested lists, search controls, file presentation, duration/time inputs).
- `elements` — atomic controls and UI-only types.
- `actions` — generic DOM behaviors.
- `icons`, `illustrations`, `branding` — portable visual assets.
- `environment` — package-wide portable platform state.
- `hosts` — dependency-inversion contracts for product behavior.

`compositions` may use every lower layer. `elements`, `actions`, `icons`,
`illustrations`, `branding`, `environment`, and `hosts` must never import
`compositions`.

## Belongs here

Presentation with credible cross-product reuse and **no** dependency on domain,
state, navigation, or infrastructure. A single current consumer is fine if reuse
is intended.

## Never here (enforced by `npm run check:architecture`)

Any import, direct or transitive, of `application`, the shell, `products`,
`features`, `datafn`, `persistence`, `schema`, `shared-state`, or `runtime`.

## Junk-drawer test

If it needs a store, navigation, a DataFn/domain type, or product branching, it
does **not** belong here. Feed those in through props or a `hosts` contract
configured by the owning application, shell, or feature layer.
# `client/shared-state` — product-independent shared client state (`@nucleum/shared-state`)

Charter: reactive state and cross-cutting ports consumed across many features,
products, extensions, and the application shell. Not UI, not infrastructure, not
a single feature's state.

Named `shared-state`, **not** `capabilities`: user-facing capabilities are
`features/` (and product surfaces). This layer is the state they share.

## Owners (import named subpaths, no root barrel)

`app-context`, `appearance`, `commands`, `events`, `files`, `notifications`,
`preferences`, `product`, `resources`, `shortcuts`.

`events` owns the focus and memory event contracts; runtime extensions own
clipper transport events. `product` exposes the configured presentation host
consumed by surfaces without importing application composition.
`resources` owns headless resource state and host contracts; connected record
actions and bulk mutations live in `features/records`.

Example: `@nucleum/shared-state/preferences/preferences.store`.

## Belongs here

State or a contract that more than one feature/product needs and that has no UI
and no product-specific workflow. Concrete command *execution* stays in
application; the command *port* lives here because everyone consumes it.

## Never here (enforced)

Any import, direct or transitive, of `application`, `features`, or `products`.
May consume `runtime`, `datafn`, `persistence`, `schema`, `utils`, and portable
UI contracts only.

## Junk-drawer test

- Renders a screen? -> a `feature/` or product surface, not here.
- Pure infrastructure with no UI? -> `runtime/`.
- State owned by one feature? -> that feature.
- Do not add a generic `shared`, `core`, `state`, or `stores` bucket; file it
  under a named owner above.
import { get, writable } from "svelte/store";
import { Display } from "@21n/ui/elements/display.enum";
import { type IViewStore } from "@21n/ui/environment/view.type";

/**
 * Programmatically set the screen size - Refer tidigit.tailwind.cjs for more details
 * @param width
 * @param height
 * @returns
 */
function calculateScreen(width: number, height: number): Display {
  let display: Display = Display.DP;
  if (width <= 600 && height <= 1000) {
    display = Display.MO;
  }
  if (width >= 600 && height >= 500) {
    display = Display.TP;
  }
  if (width >= 1024 && height >= 700) {
    display = Display.LP;
  }
  if (width >= 1500 && height >= 700) {
    display = Display.DP;
  }
  if (width >= 2000 && height >= 1000) {
    display = Display.TK;
  }
  if (width <= 600) {
    display = Display.CW;
  }
  if (width >= 4000) {
    display = Display.UW;
  }
  if (height <= 600) {
    display = Display.CH;
  }
  if (height >= 1500) {
    display = Display.VM;
  }
  return display;
}

class ViewStore {
  private readonly subject = writable<IViewStore>({
    height: 0,
    width: 0,
    landscapiness: 0,
    scale: 1,
    isPortrait: false,
    firstLoad: Date.now(),
    currentPath: "",
    isMenuHidden: false,
    display: Display.DP,
    isConstrainedWidth: false
  });
  subscribe = this.subject.subscribe;

  constructor() {
    if (typeof window !== "undefined")
      this.refresh(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);
    else this.refresh(1080, 900);
  }

  get() {
    return get(this.subject);
  }

  set(value: IViewStore) {
    this.subject.set(value);
  }

  reset(view: IViewStore) {
    this.set(view);
  }

  refresh(width: number, height: number) {
    this.subject.update((current) => {
      const next = {
        ...current,
        height: height,
        width: width,
        landscapiness: width / height,
        scale: (width / 1000 + height / 1000) / 2,
        isPortrait: false,
        isConstrainedWidth: width <= 800
      };
      next.display = calculateScreen(width, height);
      next.isPortrait = next.landscapiness < 1;
      return next;
    });
  }
}

const view = new ViewStore();
export default view;
import colorSchemes from "@21n/theme/colorschemes.json";
import type { ColorScheme } from "@21n/theme/appearance.type";
import { writable } from "svelte/store";

export interface ElementPlatform {
  embed: string;
  experiments?: Record<string, unknown>;
  isEmbed: boolean;
  isTouchDevice: boolean;
  os: string;
}

export interface ElementAppearance {
  colorScheme: ColorScheme;
}

export interface ElementLogger {
  debug(message: unknown): void;
  error(message: unknown, error?: unknown): void;
  info(message: unknown): void;
  log(message: unknown): void;
  warn(message: unknown): void;
}

const defaultColorScheme = colorSchemes[0] as ColorScheme;

/** Platform presentation state supplied by the host application. */
export const elementPlatform = writable<ElementPlatform>({
  embed: "NONE",
  isEmbed: false,
  isTouchDevice: false,
  os: "UNDETERMINED"
});

/** Theme presentation state supplied by the host application. */
export const elementAppearance = writable<ElementAppearance>({
  colorScheme: defaultColorScheme
});

/** Development presentation state supplied by the host application. */
export const elementDebugMode = writable(false);

let logger: ElementLogger = {
  debug: () => {},
  error: () => {},
  info: () => {},
  log: () => {},
  warn: () => {}
};
let haptic: () => void = () => {};
let assetPathResolver = (path: string) => path;

/** Logger facade configured by an application host. */
export const elementLogger: ElementLogger = {
  debug: (message) => logger.debug(message),
  error: (message, error) => logger.error(message, error),
  info: (message) => logger.info(message),
  log: (message) => logger.log(message),
  warn: (message) => logger.warn(message)
};

/** Updates the portable platform state without exposing host stores. */
export function syncElementPlatform(value: ElementPlatform) {
  elementPlatform.set(value);
}

/** Updates the portable appearance state without exposing host stores. */
export function syncElementAppearance(value: ElementAppearance) {
  elementAppearance.set(value);
}

/** Updates development-only element presentation. */
export function syncElementDebugMode(value: boolean) {
  elementDebugMode.set(value);
}

/** Installs the host logger used by portable elements. */
export function configureElementLogger(value: ElementLogger) {
  logger = value;
}

/** Installs optional host interaction feedback. */
export function configureElementHaptic(value: () => void) {
  haptic = value;
}

/** Installs portable asset URL resolution supplied by the host application. */
export function configureElementAssetPath(value: (path: string) => string) {
  assetPathResolver = value;
}

/** Resolves an application-hosted asset without coupling UI to product storage. */
export function resolveElementAssetPath(path: string) {
  return assetPathResolver(path);
}

/** Requests interaction feedback when the host supports it. */
export function elementHaptic() {
  haptic();
}
