     1	# `client/shell` — application shell: arrangement and navigation (`@nucleum/shell`)
     2	
     3	Charter: how the app is arranged and moved through, independent of what content
     4	fills it. Pure "where things go and how you move", never "what a screen does".
     5	
     6	## Owners
     7	
     8	`navigation` (URL/history, resource navigation), `topNav`, `bottomNav`,
     9	`leftPanel`, `rightPanel`, `trail`, `layers` (theme, metadata, embed),
    10	`overlays`, `modal`, `paint` (page and
    11	resource resolvers fed through the shared-state action renderer), `split views`,
    12	`tabs`, `sync` and `notifications` chrome.
    13	
    14	`navigation/NavigationLayout.svelte` owns route-driven arrangement and receives
    15	connected nav snippets from application. `overlays/ModalLayer.svelte` owns the
    16	overlay stack and resolves action content through the registered renderer.
    17	
    18	## Belongs here
    19	
    20	Anything that owns URL state, panel arrangement, tab/sidebar behavior, product
    21	menus, or shell events. If removing it would not change what any single screen
    22	does, only how screens are framed and reached, it belongs here.
    23	
    24	## Not here
    25	
    26	- Domain screens and workflows (account, library, settings, command) ->
    27	  `surfaces/`.
    28	- Portable domain-free UI -> `ui/`.
    29	- Content capabilities -> `features/`.
    30	- Sync scheduling -> `datafn/visibility-sync`; telemetry mechanics ->
    31	  `runtime/telemetry`; consent/lifecycle wiring -> application layers;
    32	  connected support -> `surfaces/help/support`.
    33	- Application composition layers that wire the running product together
    34	  (base/user layers, the action `ComponentResolver`, `AppLoadingView`, and the
    35	  final settings action assembly) -> `application/`.
    36	
    37	## Dependency direction (enforced)
    38	
    39	Shell is acyclic: it must not import `application/`, `surfaces/`, or
    40	`products/`, directly or transitively. Product navigation config enters through
    41	`@nucleum/shared-state/product/product-config-host`; concrete chrome
    42	(brand/logo, account avatar, search input, bulk-edit bar, offline status,
    43	capture, profile section) enters through optional Svelte snippet props provided
    44	by the application chrome adapters (`client/composition/chrome/`).
    45	
    46	## Junk-drawer test
    47	
    48	A shell component may read navigation and shell state, but it must not contain a
    49	feature workflow. If it orchestrates a domain task (sign-in, billing, resource
    50	browsing), it is a surface, not shell.
     1	# `client/runtime` — browser infrastructure, no UI
     2	
     3	Charter: how the client talks to the outside world and computes, with no
     4	presentation and no product workflow. It sits at the bottom and may be imported
     5	by everyone, including extensions and workers that never load the full app.
     6	
     7	## Owners
     8	
     9	`account` (session state + transport), `audio`, `connectivity`, `embed`,
    10	`inference`, `logging`, `os`, `context`.
    11	
    12	## Belongs here
    13	
    14	Transport, network authority, native/embed messaging, inference, audio decoding,
    15	diagnostics, and the bare reactive state those need. Pure, low-dependency,
    16	changes rarely.
    17	
    18	## Never here (enforced)
    19	
    20	Any import of `features`, `products`, `application`, the shell, `shared-state`,
    21	or portable UI. Runtime is a leaf that others depend on, not the reverse.
    22	
    23	## Junk-drawer test
    24	
    25	- Has Svelte/DOM UI? -> not runtime.
    26	- Coordinates a user-facing workflow (redirects, screens, prompts)? -> that
    27	  workflow belongs in `application` or a feature; keep only the primitive here.
